{"agent_id":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:50:33.040768134Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"36ca7a67-bf3a-41d3-8648-353118bdde58","comment_uuid":"f284eadd-c93e-483a-95b4-e656fc3aa428","author":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","content":"FINDINGS (1/4) — attribution & correlation (BLOCKING)\n\nF1 — Attribution is the load-bearing assumption and is unverified.\n- statement: The whole mechanism attributes each shared-log line to an agent. The proposal itself states 'S2 fork binary writes it, v2 TUI logging behavior unverified' and 'shared single log file needs attribution mapping.' No evidence is offered that the log carries a stable per-agent/session token, nor a mapping to a worktree/agent.\n- why-it-matters: If lines can't be attributed, PARKED-RETRYING/STREAM-DEATH/SPIRAL are misrouted; a misattributed kill hits the WRONG agent; the evidence bundle is also corrupted, defeating audit. Adopt/reject turns on this.\n- cheapest-test: Get one real multi-agent opencode.log from BOTH producers; confirm (a) a per-line session/agent token exists, (b) stable for agent lifetime, (c) maps to a discoverable agent (worktree/.kickoff-metadata). Any failure => design cannot proceed as specified.\n- severity: MUST FIX (blocking).\n\nF2 — STREAM-DEATH request-correlation is unspecified.\n- statement: 'unresolved-request aging past threshold' requires correlating a request-issued event with its resolution for the SAME request. No correlation key (request ID? call UUID? recency heuristic?) is given.\n- why-it-matters: Without it, 'unresolved' is indistinguishable from 'slow but healthy mid-call.' The motivating deepseek case was 'request issued, never resolved, zero errors' — but if no request ID exists, the watcher can't know two lines are one request, so it either never detects death or false-positives on every slow call.\n- cheapest-test: Inspect real logs for a request/call identifier present in both issue and completion lines. If absent, STREAM-DEATH collapses to a last-activity timeout — which the existing poll already does, so eventing adds nothing for this class.\n- severity: MUST FIX (blocking for STREAM-DEATH class).","created_at":"2026-08-24T01:50:33.034115317Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAjCbtC4RYwEe2jbwCY325F0ZaW7Cdt2c2oa4dusHsZObPprd0y00Qs5yvb3kW0Pnm41amG8GmCz6qBk/phNpxCw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCFYburxNx8jVncmytG3G1pYw6i0V39uUJUUWQxM9QcgaBNU78rwcpGfta26Ek4RNzKU8WTVhGo5Nrtg9RA+dg8="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-24T01:50:42.045122799Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"36ca7a67-bf3a-41d3-8648-353118bdde58","comment_uuid":"365b460c-5f7f-4a7a-8c87-d5fc2f783777","author":"pp3g-4eBL-clean-room-adversarial-review-on-444-you-are-one-of","content":"FINDINGS (2/4) — parser, spiral false-positives, kill trust (BLOCKING for auto-kill)\n\nF3 — Parser built on one night's inferred strings, not a schema.\n- statement: Keys on 'AI_APICallError'+'retry-after' and 'request issued, never resolved, zero errors' — forensic observations, not a specified contract; v2 TUI behavior admitted unverified.\n- why-it-matters: Real wording varies (RateLimitError, 429, quota_exceeded, upstream connect error, stream closed, context deadline exceeded). A parser matching only observed strings silently misses most real failures — the worst mode for a safety mechanism (false negative = the exact death it was built to catch goes undetected).\n- cheapest-test: Build an error/stream corpus from both producers across failure types; measure parser coverage; add an 'unrecognized-line-rate' alert for schema drift.\n- severity: HIGH (MUST FIX before trusting classifications; acceptable only behind shadow-mode).\n\nF4 — Spiral auto-kill false-positive risk on legitimate verbose tasks.\n- statement: SPIRAL = 'repetition-ratio over trailing window with no fresh commits/checkpoints => automatic kill after one confirmation cycle.' Metric, window, threshold unspecified; only guardrail is 'BOTH high similarity AND no progress signals.'\n- why-it-matters: Asymmetric risk. A false-positive kill destroys an agent's in-progress (possibly uncommitted) work — irreversible. A false-negative only costs tokens and is caught by the poll backstop. The proposal's own deepseek '25-min invisible churn' example is exactly the long repetitive-looking activity that could trip a naive detector yet may be real work. Test-suite output, build warnings, large diffs, code-gen loops routinely emit high-similarity lines >90s without a commit.\n- cheapest-test: Labeled corpus of (a) good verbose runs and (b) real spirals; find a threshold separating them with ~zero false positives on (a); run detector in SHADOW mode (WOULD-KILL, no kill) across real agents for a defined period; count false positives before any kill is authorized.\n- severity: MUST FIX (auto-kill authority should not be granted until shadow-mode false-positive rate is demonstrated near-zero).\n\nF11 — Trust basis for automatic kills is thin.\n- statement: Auto-kill is 'operator-granted' but rests on a one-night corpus and an unverified classifier (F1–F3). No shadow-mode, no kill rate-limit, no human-override path stated.\n- why-it-matters: A wrong classifier with kill authority destroys work irreversibly; at scale a single parser bug could nuke a whole swarm. Trust basis must be: demonstrated precision on labeled corpus + shadow burn-in + per-window kill cap (e.g., <=1 kill/10min) + always-available manual disable.\n- cheapest-test: Mandate shadow-mode phase (emit WOULD-KILL+evidence, no kill) for a defined period; require zero false positives on labeled data; then enable kills behind a rate cap + global kill-disable switch.\n- severity: MUST FIX (blocking for the auto-kill grant).","created_at":"2026-08-24T01:50:42.036432403Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAQWw5yteU9MmlkWMmPciS09b49nEdLVWLixrz+GT+eJ6hYtV0Dcg/7b3fMSmQjJWk1W82t2OWOzZD8kAEytjPDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:usl0k0EVKIRzWIYxQlgcjiM/cGQ8uEjxBXwkMq/YBro","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgCLvCYlub0EX1P/3vBtfMaCQEYV65ygOLwZSOiPTrhK4AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLhMGovpBYYSpSSEDBWdCYTId0VLasw44h7CNTtYLmJC/h83DFzVoORGdHx8mGqH150vdA0xgciDaQuqSFXCdA8="}
